- Receive Vouchers
- Journal Vouchers
- Cheque Management
- Chart of Accounts
- Customer Ledgers
- Supplier Ledgers
- General Ledger
- Cash Book
- Trial Balance
- Financial Reports
- Stock Reports
- Recovery Reports
- Settings
- Audit Logs
- Backup Management
3. Use Firebase Authentication with email and password. Disable public registration. Allow the owner to create authorized staff accounts.
4. Use Cloud Firestore for persistent business data. All records must be associated with a showroom ID.
5. Implement role-based access control and secure database rules.
6. Build modular, reusable components and maintain a clean folder architecture.
7. Design all forms with proper validation, loading states, error messages and success notifications.
8. Use professional financial formatting with PKR currency support.
9. Ensure responsive desktop, tablet and mobile layouts.
10. Implement server-side business logic for financial transactions. Never rely exclusively on frontend calculations or permissions.
11. Create an accounting architecture based on balanced double-entry journal transactions.
12. Prevent duplicate invoice submissions, unauthorized edits and accidental financial deletions.
13. Use audit logs for sensitive operations.
14. Create reusable reporting, filtering, searching and PDF/Excel export utilities.
IMPORTANT DEVELOPMENT RULES:
- Do not create fake functionality.
- Do not use localStorage as the primary business database.
- Do not use hardcoded sample values as live business data.
- Do not create buttons that have no working actions.
- Do not silently ignore failed database operations.
- Keep all financial operations consistent.
- Build the application in modules.
- Preserve existing functionality when adding new modules.
- Verify every module before marking it complete.
FIRST TASK:
Set up the project architecture, Firebase integration, authentication, database structure, security foundation, reusable UI components and main ERP dashboard.

Do not attempt to implement every business module in this first phase. Build a stable foundation first and then implement each module incrementally.




